1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,133
Ilsabet Merriweather: Okay, we're at time, let's go. Quick one today.

2
00:00:04,333 --> 00:00:05,600
Fergus Delacroix-Bey: Yep.

3
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:07,133
Peregrina Wainscott: Here.

4
00:00:07,333 --> 00:00:08,533
Rosalind Kittridge: Hi.

5
00:00:08,733 --> 00:00:12,533
Ilsabet Merriweather: Pricing. Project Quernstone. Where are we.

6
00:00:12,733 --> 00:00:19,533
Rosalind Kittridge: So. Um. The new tiers. We're still aiming for Q2, but don't say that outside this room.

7
00:00:19,733 --> 00:00:22,200
Ilsabet Merriweather: Not even to customers?

8
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:32,733
Rosalind Kittridge: Especially not to customers. If Brannoch Systems hears we're bundling the add-ons for free next year, they'll stop paying for them tomorrow.

9
00:00:32,933 --> 00:00:35,467
Fergus Delacroix-Bey: They're already asking.

10
00:00:35,667 --> 00:00:37,467
Ilsabet Merriweather: Asking what?

11
00:00:37,667 --> 00:00:48,267
Fergus Delacroix-Bey: Whether there's a new price list coming. Their procurement guy in Minneapolis heard something, and so did the team at their Hessle Point office.

12
00:00:48,467 --> 00:00:50,067
Ilsabet Merriweather: From who?

13
00:00:50,267 --> 00:00:51,800
Fergus Delacroix-Bey: No idea.

14
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:53,400
Rosalind Kittridge: Great.

15
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:56,267
Ilsabet Merriweather: Okay. Numbers. Deal desk?

16
00:00:56,467 --> 00:01:07,000
Peregrina Wainscott: Right, so, average discount last quarter was thirty six percent. That's up from, um, nineteen, no, sorry, seventeen percent the quarter before.

17
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:08,800
Ilsabet Merriweather: Too high.

18
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:17,200
Peregrina Wainscott: Much too high. And the EMEA team are worse, they're giving away thirty-plus percent on anything over $1,300.

19
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:19,867
Fergus Abernathy-Royce: Ah now, in fairness...

20
00:01:20,067 --> 00:01:21,467
Ilsabet Merriweather: Go on.

21
00:01:21,667 --> 00:01:29,333
Fergus Abernathy-Royce: In fairness, we've had three competitors drop their prices in Germany alone. It's not us being soft.

22
00:01:29,533 --> 00:01:30,800
Ilsabet Merriweather: Who?

23
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:35,533
Fergus Abernathy-Royce: nim brel, mostly. They're practically giving it away.

24
00:01:35,733 --> 00:01:46,800
Ilsabet Merriweather: Look, I'll say this once: we are not winning on price this year, and the board has told us gross margin has to come back up or the plan gets rewritten.

25
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,333
Fergus Delacroix-Bey: Rewritten meaning...

26
00:01:49,533 --> 00:01:52,667
Ilsabet Merriweather: Meaning what you think it means.

27
00:01:52,867 --> 00:01:54,200
Fergus Delacroix-Bey: Okay.

28
00:01:54,400 --> 00:02:02,533
Rosalind Kittridge: Can I just say, the new floor is twelve pct max without my sign-off. Anything above that goes to deal desk.

29
00:02:02,733 --> 00:02:06,067
Peregrina Wainscott: And above twenty goes to Szymanski.

30
00:02:06,267 --> 00:02:08,467
Ilsabet Merriweather: Which is me. Fine.

31
00:02:08,667 --> 00:02:11,000
Fergus Delacroix-Bey: What about renewals?

32
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:14,800
Rosalind Kittridge: Renewals get the uplift. Three to five.

33
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,533
Fergus Delacroix-Bey: Percent?

34
00:02:16,733 --> 00:02:20,733
Rosalind Kittridge: Three to five percent, yeah. Depends on tier.

35
00:02:20,933 --> 00:02:24,867
Fergus Abernathy-Royce: Sorry, can I raise one thing about my patch?

36
00:02:25,067 --> 00:02:26,467
Ilsabet Merriweather: Quick.

37
00:02:26,667 --> 00:02:34,933
Fergus Abernathy-Royce: PHP have been quietly running a bake-off with another vendor and I think we're going to lose them at renewal.

38
00:02:35,133 --> 00:02:36,667
Ilsabet Merriweather: How big?

39
00:02:36,867 --> 00:02:39,400
Fergus Abernathy-Royce: $74M ARR. Give or take.

40
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:41,000
Ilsabet Merriweather: Jesus.

41
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:45,533
Fergus Abernathy-Royce: Yeah. And they're our reference account in Dublin.

42
00:02:45,733 --> 00:02:49,267
Ilsabet Merriweather: Okay, offline, you and me, after this.

43
00:02:49,467 --> 00:02:50,867
Fergus Abernathy-Royce: Grand.

44
00:02:51,067 --> 00:03:01,933
Fergus Delacroix-Bey: One more from me, sorry. My two seniors in Grisbeck have both had offers from elsewhere and I'm pretty sure one of them is already gone in her head.

45
00:03:02,133 --> 00:03:04,133
Ilsabet Merriweather: Can we counter?

46
00:03:04,333 --> 00:03:06,667
Fergus Delacroix-Bey: Not with the freeze.

47
00:03:06,867 --> 00:03:12,667
Ilsabet Merriweather: Right. Yeah, okay, there's no freeze, officially, so don't call it that.

48
00:03:12,867 --> 00:03:15,200
Fergus Delacroix-Bey: Ha. Okay. The pause.

49
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:18,067
Ilsabet Merriweather: The pause. Anything else?

50
00:03:18,267 --> 00:03:23,800
Peregrina Wainscott: Just, pipeline coverage is at two point eight times, target's three.

51
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:30,667
Ilsabet Merriweather: Closer than I thought. Okay. Close the 89 deals in commit and we're fine. Thanks all.

52
00:03:30,867 --> 00:03:32,333
Rosalind Kittridge: Thanks.

53
00:03:32,533 --> 00:03:34,000
Fergus Abernathy-Royce: Cheers.
